/*!
@defgroup modcon MODCON Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides APIs for MCUXpresso SDK devices' Module
Controller (MODCON) operation.

MODCON manages per-IP access control (trust mask, domain mask, locks),
peripheral reset, and per-IP configuration / status registers. It also
implements the device-side `RESET_PeripheralReset()` entry point used by
the generic SDK reset interface.

The MODCON driver supports:
  - Reading the MODCON version register and trust mask
  - Setting the MODCON trust mask with optional lock
  - Per-IP domain-access mask programming with optional lock
  - Issuing and clearing per-IP reset requests, plus a one-shot peripheral
    reset (assert + de-assert) sequence used by the SDK reset interface
  - Per-IP CFG[idx] read / write and per-IP STATUS[idx] read

This component also exposes IP enumerations for ASRC, SPDIF, SAI, PDM,
FREQME, EDMA3 / EDMA5, NPU, SRAMCTL, NIC, ROMCP, ENET, ENET_QOS, USDHC,
XSPI / XSPIR, I3C, LPSPI, LPI2C, LPUART, FlexCAN, EQDC, GPIO, LPIT, FlexIO,
FlexPWM, SINC, CRC, IOMUXC, CGUA / CGUANA, STM, DAC, QTMR, ADC, MIPI_CSI /
MIPI_DSI, ISI, DCIF, JPEG, GPU, REFORMATTER, CSI, LPTMR, EWM, SWT, ACMP,
PMUANA and CGU.

*/
